Spec: SpecDD Reference Rename Handler

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Route rename actions invoked from explicit SpecDD `@` symbol references to the resolved IntelliJ PSI target.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDReferenceRenameHandler.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDReferenceRenameHandler.kt

Can read:
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/references/SpecDDReferenceRenameHandlerBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Activate only inside SpecDD files.
  Activate only when the caret is on a resolved `@SpecDDSymbolReference`.
  Use the referenced PSI target as the element being renamed.
  Use the SpecDD reference element as the rename context.
  Delegate the actual rename refactor to IntelliJ PSI rename support.
  Preserve full SpecDD reference text by relying on `@SpecDDSymbolReference.handleElementRename`.
  Handle caret positions at the reference end by checking the previous offset.
  Stay independent from language-specific plugins.

Must not:
  Rename unresolved symbol references.
  Claim rename for path references, glob references, plain prose, or non-SpecDD files.
